          dealing: 'Each player receives 7 cards face-down. One card is turned up to start the discard pile. Remaining cards form the stock.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Win the pot by having the highest-ranking 4ndcard 'Going Down' hand and 3ndcard 'Coming Back' hand.",
          gameplay: "1. Turning: Players take turns (clockwise) drawing one card from either the stock or discard pile, then discarding one card.\n2. Duration: The game lasts exactly SIX rounds. After the dealer's sixth turn, the play ends.\n3. Showdown: Players divide their 7 cards into a 4ndcard hand and a 3ndcard hand. They show the 4ndcard hands first to determine the winner, then the 3ndcard hands.",
          keyRules: [
            'Aces are always low (A-2-3-4 is valid, J-Q-KndA is NOT).',
            'Hand Ties: If two players tie for the best hand, they cut cards from the deck; the higher cut wins.',
            "The pot is often split between the winner of the 'Going Down' hand and the 'Coming Back' hand.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'In early rounds, focus on your 4ndcard hand, as it is harder to complete and often represents a larger portion of the pot.',
          intermediate: "Waste management: If you draw a high card (King/Queen) that doesn't fit your runs, keep it as a 'High Card' kicker for a pair rather than letting opponents pick it up from the discard pile.",
          advanced: 'Round Counting: Since you only have 6 turns, if by turn 4 you have no pairs or runs, pivot immediately to building a high-card flush or a simple high-card hand to salvage one of the sub-pots.',
          tips: [
            "Don't ignore the 3ndcard hand. A simple Prial (3-of-a-kind) in the 3ndcard slot is almost unbeatable.",
            'Watch what opponents pick from the discard pile. If they pick a 7, do not discard a 6 or 8.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
